# Two charts of a board on one figure. The board draws its left chart's line, which makes the left chart's figure, and the
# left chart lends it to the right one by its own `lend`: `self.left.lend(self.right)` runs on the board through `left` and
# fills `other` with the board through `right` (#172), so inside `lend`, `other.take(self.fig, self.ax)` runs on the
# board's right part, handed its left part's `fig` and `ax`. A parameter filled through a projection is that projection
# (#173): `take` sets the fields of the right part, which a chart keeps its figure in (`Node::holds` says the board's
# `right` holds a Chart), to those of the left part. From then on the right part holds the left part's figure, and its
# line draws on it: the screen shows one figure, named by the part that made it.

route notebooks.overlay
step overlay/overlay
step overlay/overlay/Chart()
step overlay/overlay/Chart()#2
step overlay/overlay/Board()
step overlay/overlay/Board.overlay
step overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line
choice overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line/?1
step overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line/?1/Chart.create_figure
step overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend
step overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend/Chart.take
step overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2
choice overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2/?1
step overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2/?1/Chart.create_figure

line entry > overlay call
line overlay/overlay/Chart() > Chart@overlay/overlay/Chart() value
line overlay/overlay/Chart()#2 > Chart@overlay/overlay/Chart()#2 value
line Chart@overlay/overlay/Chart() > overlay/overlay/Board() value          # `self.left = left`
line Chart@overlay/overlay/Chart()#2 > overlay/overlay/Board() value        # `self.right = right`
line overlay/overlay/Board() > Board·board@overlay/overlay/Board() value

# the left chart's line, run on the board through `left`, makes the figure
line Board·board@overlay/overlay/Board() > overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line/?1/Chart.create_figure value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line/?1/Chart.create_figure > Chart·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line/?1 value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line/?1/Chart.create_figure > Figure 1 · Board · board.left own   # `plt.subplots()`
line Chart·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line/?1 > overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line > Board·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line value

# the left lends it to the right: `take` runs on the board's right part, handed its left part's fields
line Board·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line > overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend/Chart.take value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend/Chart.take > Chart·other@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend/Chart.take value   # `self.fig, self.ax = fig, ax`
line Chart·other@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend/Chart.take > overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend > Board·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend value

# the right chart's line draws on the figure its part now holds
line Board·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.lend > overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2/?1/Chart.create_figure value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2/?1/Chart.create_figure > Chart·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2/?1 value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2/?1/Chart.create_figure > Figure 1 · Board · board.left own   # the figure the right part took
line Chart·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2/?1 > overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2 value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2 > Board·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2 value
line Board·self@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay/Chart.line#2 > overlay/overlay/Board.overlay value
line overlay/overlay/Board.overlay > Board·board@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay value
line Board·board@overlay/overlay/Board.overlay > overlay/overlay value     # `return board`
line overlay/overlay > Board·board@overlay/overlay value                   # `board = overlay(..)`

home Chart@overlay/overlay/Chart() overlay/overlay
home Chart@overlay/overlay/Chart()#2 overlay/overlay
home Board·board@overlay/overlay/Board() overlay/overlay
